1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,710
Gus is stuck floating in space,

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,340
ten feet from his ship, and

3
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:04,680
the only rocket he has is

4
00:00:04,690 --> 00:00:05,120
a fart.

5
00:00:05,174 --> 00:00:06,974
It's two in the afternoon, high

6
00:00:06,984 --> 00:00:08,704
above the ocean, and his safety

7
00:00:08,714 --> 00:00:09,944
rope just came loose.

8
00:00:09,998 --> 00:00:10,358
He kicks.

9
00:00:10,368 --> 00:00:11,028
He swims.

10
00:00:11,038 --> 00:00:11,628
Nothing.

11
00:00:11,808 --> 00:00:13,158
In space, there's nothing to push

12
00:00:13,168 --> 00:00:13,498
on.

13
00:00:13,552 --> 00:00:15,462
His wife radios, throw something!

14
00:00:15,712 --> 00:00:17,142
His neighbor says he's a goner.

15
00:00:17,186 --> 00:00:18,336
Gus says he had beans for

16
00:00:18,346 --> 00:00:20,506
lunch, turns around, and fires.

17
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,590
Let's be kind and say it

18
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,050
all shoots straight out the back.

19
00:00:23,094 --> 00:00:24,224
Now Gus is moving.

20
00:00:24,414 --> 00:00:25,494
One hair's width a minute.

21
00:00:25,548 --> 00:00:26,898
At that pace, ten feet takes

22
00:00:26,908 --> 00:00:27,838
over three weeks.

23
00:00:28,058 --> 00:00:29,578
He has air for eight hours.

24
00:00:29,622 --> 00:00:30,262
But wait.

25
00:00:30,272 --> 00:00:31,792
Rockets run on gas too.

26
00:00:31,802 --> 00:00:33,082
So why is his so weak?

27
00:00:33,136 --> 00:00:34,596
You see, a rocket moves by

28
00:00:34,606 --> 00:00:35,786
throwing stuff away.

29
00:00:36,106 --> 00:00:37,436
What counts is how much, and

30
00:00:37,446 --> 00:00:38,166
how fast.

31
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:39,540
Ever stood on a skateboard and

32
00:00:39,550 --> 00:00:40,860
thrown a heavy backpack?

33
00:00:41,090 --> 00:00:42,290
You roll the other way.

34
00:00:42,334 --> 00:00:43,464
A fart is a tenth of

35
00:00:43,474 --> 00:00:45,214
a gram of gas, leaving at

36
00:00:45,224 --> 00:00:46,184
ten feet a second.

37
00:00:46,238 --> 00:00:47,678
Gus and his suit weigh four

38
00:00:47,688 --> 00:00:48,878
hundred sixty pounds.

39
00:00:48,932 --> 00:00:50,162
So he pulls off a slipper,

40
00:00:50,172 --> 00:00:51,372
and throws it, hard.

41
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:52,846
Half a pound at twenty miles

42
00:00:52,856 --> 00:00:53,486
an hour.

43
00:00:53,756 --> 00:00:55,356
That's six thousand times the push

44
00:00:55,366 --> 00:00:55,886
of a fart.

45
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:57,790
Luckily, five minutes later, Gus

46
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,120
floats in through the hatch.

47
00:00:59,174 --> 00:01:00,404
Unluckily, a spacesuit is

48
00:01:00,414 --> 00:01:00,894
airtight.

49
00:01:00,948 --> 00:01:02,288
So the fart never left.

50
00:01:02,488 --> 00:01:04,008
It rode home with him, inside

51
00:01:04,018 --> 00:01:04,728
the helmet.
